                <pb facs="0471" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg376"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8339: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-13T17:00:00+08:00">November 13, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>545. Embassy’s 537, November 9, 5 p.m. Fighting is reported by press to have
                    broken out on the Chahar–Suiyuan border on November 11 when an attack was
                    launched on Suiyuan by the pro-Manchukuo forces of Li Shou Hsin at Shangtu, west
                    of Chahar. Confirmation or details are not available.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tokyo, Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
